PARITY — the native surface reproduces the web TimelineScrubber data, composition, states & i18n:
[x] Interactive track (content): thin track + buffered band + neon fill + active playhead thumb
    (grows + accent ring while dragging) + hover ghost playhead + 8 marker-kind ticks (tint by kind,
    clustered-count badge, tap-to-seek, `.help` tooltip) + hover/drag preview bubble (time over the
    host-formatted speed/power/SoC/elevation) + optional decorative background (web `<Sparkline>`).
[x] Drag-to-scrub emits intermediate seeks throttled to SCRUB_INTERVAL_MS (0.05s); a zero-distance
    drag = tap-to-seek on release; VoiceOver swipe = adjustable slider increment/decrement.
[x] Reduce Motion drops the fill/thumb transition (web `prefers-reduced-motion`) via
    @Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion). useTranslation → P1/S10 facade.
[x] P4 leaf states the web pure render lacks: loading (skeleton track), empty (no timeline → friendly),
    error (QueryError + retry), plus the orthogonal freshness axis: stale/offline chip + banner with a
    one-shot stale auto-refresh.
[x] Hooks bind via the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam (TimelineScrubberSource + TimelineScrubberModel);
    NO direct HTTP in the view (web source has none).
[x] i18n: 22/22 keys present in TimelineScrubber.strings (table "TimelineScrubber"); web parity keys
    `Playback progress`→timelineScrubber.progress, `at {{pct}}%`→timelineScrubber.markerAtPercent.
    No English string literals in native code (all via the P1/S10 facade).
[x] Accessibility on every interactive element: the track is one adjustable slider (label + m:ss/`NN%`
    value + increment/decrement); each marker is a focusable Button with a localized label (+clustered
    count) and a tooltip.
[x] Telemetry: `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "TimelineScrubber" (P1/S11 seam;
    asserted by testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnce).
[x] No TODO/stub/mock/placeholder/Lorem in shipped code.

